WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.490
Picture a valley full of rabbits.

2
00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:05.230
One good year, rabbit numbers boom.

3
00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:08.390
A little later, fox numbers boom too.

4
00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:12.810
Then the rabbits crash, and
soon after, so do the foxes.

5
00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:16.390
Year after year, the two
populations rise and fall,

6
00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.610
one just behind the other.

7
00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:21.610
Why would predator and prey
chase each other round in cycles

8
00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:22.910
like this?

9
00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:26.430
In this mission, you'll read
predator–prey graphs and compare

10
00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:27.750
where the peaks fall.

11
00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:31.530
You'll find out how ecologists
estimate a population they can't

12
00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:34.030
count one by one, using quadrats.

13
00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:38.230
And you'll use transects to see
how a species changes across a

14
00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:39.470
habitat.

15
00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:43.210
Your mission: explain why predator
and prey numbers rise and

16
00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:44.970
fall in cycles.
